# -*- mode:org; coding:utf-8 -*-
#+TITLE: deferred-nod-default-contents -- what cador still leaves out of a new drawing's default objects
#+STATUS: DONE
#+PRIORITY: P3
#+TYPE: feature
#+DEPENDS: cador-entget-subclass-layout-and-record-pointers
#+BRANCH: -
#+DATE: 2026-10-24

* Context

clautolisp 2.3.52 made the NOD's default containers; 2.3.53 fills them with
what entget-pointers section 12 dumped (AutoCAD 2022 job 17440097863,
BricsCAD V25 Windows 17440097864, V26 macOS 17440097865 -- the two BricsCADs
identical): cador/source/default-objects.lisp, generated by
scripts/gen-default-objects.py from those results. Vendor documentation
gives the object formats, not a fresh drawing's contents (searched
2026-10-24: only the AutoLISP help's sample listing, "About Dictionary
Objects and Entries", which says not to rely on it).

Both runners' templates are French and metric (layouts Presentation1/2,
mleader style Annotatif on AutoCAD, Metric50 view styles, acadiso.lin): the
contents are the template's. The generator renames the paper layouts to
cador's Layout1 / Layout2; everything else is as measured.

* Deferred

1. Extension dictionaries of the objects INSIDE the NOD (AutoCAD's Model
   layout, its three materials, the Standard table style; BricsCAD's detail
   / section view styles): section 12 opened only those of the NOD, the
   records and the TABLE objects. Measure them (one more level), then make
   them.
2. The layer record's 348 (AutoCAD), the BLOCK's 71 (BricsCAD), the
   BLOCK_RECORD's 360 / 340 / {BLKREFS 331 ...} groups.
3. Another template (English / imperial) would give other names and values;
   if a dialect ever needs to follow one, measure it with section 12.
4. Saving: the DXF writer puts every object of the entities table in
   ENTITIES (libredwg drops them from a DWG; the entities survive -- checked
   with a template drawing holding the 87 default objects) and writes only
   the legacy struct dictionary tree in OBJECTS; a DXF-loaded drawing's NOD
   is not what (namedobjdict) reaches. The handle-addressed objects should go
   to OBJECTS, and a loaded NOD become the handle-addressed one.

* Done (clautolisp 2.3.54)

Section 12, round 2 (AutoCAD 2022 job 17441114651, BricsCAD V25 17441114652,
V26 17441114653) dumped the member extension dictionaries and the records'
values.

1. Member extension dictionaries: AutoCAD's Model layout and Standard table
   style (empty), its three materials (FBXASSET XRECORDs; Global also
   BUMPTILE / DIFFUSETILE / OPACITYTILE / REFLECTIONTILE); BricsCAD's detail /
   section view styles (empty). Generated as each object's 5th element and
   made owned by it; the {ACAD_REACTORS} group sits after the
   {ACAD_XDICTIONARY} one on AutoCAD, before it on BricsCAD, as measured.
2. Layer 0's 348 points at an ERASED object on AutoCAD (none on BricsCAD):
   nothing to show, left out. BLOCK: BricsCAD's 71 is 0; a space's BLOCK
   lists its layout (410 Model / Layout1); AutoCAD's 1 is the block's name
   for a block, "" for a space. BLOCK_RECORD: 2 360 (its BLOCK) 340 (a
   space's LAYOUT; erased for another block on AutoCAD, absent on BricsCAD)
   {BLKREFS 331 ...} (its INSERTs) 70 280 281 -- and a block record holding a
   BLOCK header no longer shows the BLOCK's 10 / 70 as its own.
3. Another template: not measurable from the runners (both French, metric);
   kept as a limit of the data, see Context. Not a task.
4. Saving: the DXF writer puts the handle-addressed objects in OBJECTS, the
   root first, not in ENTITIES; the loader makes a file's OBJECTS
   handle-addressed objects (flagged OBJECT-P, never graphical) and its first
   dictionary the root, so (namedobjdict) reaches a loaded NOD and a
   template drawing keeps its own. DXF and DWG round trips of a template
   drawing keep the NOD (16 entries + one added XRECORD and its value).
   DRAWING-ENTITY-COUNT counts graphical entities only. Test
   DXF-ROUND-TRIP-KEEPS-HANDLE-ADDRESSED-OBJECTS.

Not modelled: a space's empty-block ENDBLK (its -2 on the vendors; see
deferred-spec-research.issue).
